      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "The force required to loosen a bolt varies inversely with the length of the handle of the wrench used. This means that the product of the force and the length of the handle is a constant. We can set up the equation:\n\nForce * Length = Constant\n\nWe are given that a wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force to loosen the bolt. We can use this information to find the constant:\n\n375 * 9 = Constant\n\nThe constant is 3375. Now, we need to find the length of the handle that will require 15 inches of force to loosen the same bolt. We can set up the equation:\n\nForce * Length = Constant\n\nLet x be the length of the handle that requires 15 inches of force. We can substitute the known values into the equation:\n\n15 * x = 3375\n\nNow, we can solve for x:\n\nx = 3375 / 15\n\nx = 225\n\nTherefore, a wrench with a handle length of 15 inches will require 225 pounds of force to loosen the same bolt.",
